  "display_name": "Toyota Camry Hybrid (2018+) — EXPERIMENTAL",
  "description": "Best-effort Mode 21 hybrid coverage for the 8th-generation Camry Hybrid (XV70, 2018+) and the 9th-generation hybrid-only Camry (2025+). Both share the TNGA-K platform and THS-II hybrid drivetrain (FWD; no rear motor) with the 2020 Lexus RX 450h. This profile inherits the high-confidence hybrid PIDs validated against Nathan's RX 450hL — MG1/MG2 torques (PIDs 61/62), HV pack voltage (PID 98), four battery cell-block temperatures (PID 95) — minus the rear-motor PID since Camry Hybrid is FWD only. Includes additional candidate PIDs (SOC real/display, MG RPMs) from generic-toyota-hybrid that may or may not respond on this platform; auto-demoted if not. UNVALIDATED on real Camry hardware; treat as a starting point.",
